---
import LegalLayout from '@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { firm, offer, firmPolicyLinks } from '@/config/site';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="Terms governing use of the Hoffman Legal demand letter website."
>
  <!-- Draft for attorney review before launch. -->
  <p>
    By using this website you agree to these terms.
    {
      firmPolicyLinks.terms ? (
        <>
          They supplement {firm.name}’s <a href={firmPolicyLinks.terms}>firm-wide terms</a>.
        </>
      ) : null
    }
  </p>

  <h2>Information only</h2>
  <p>
    Content on this website is general information about {firm.name}’s demand letter service. It is not legal advice,
    and it may not reflect the most current legal developments.
  </p>

  <h2>Inquiries and representation</h2>
  <p>
    Submitting a request is an inquiry only. It is not an engagement agreement and does not create an attorney-client
    relationship. {firm.name} may decline any matter. Representation begins only after acceptance, a conflict check and a
    signed engagement agreement, which governs the scope of the representation.
  </p>

  <h2>Fees</h2>
  <p>
    The {offer.priceDisplay} fee applies to one attorney-prepared demand letter in a matter accepted for this service.
    {offer.payment.noUpfront} Work outside the standard service, including litigation, is not included and requires a
    separate agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>No guarantee</h2>
  <p>
    {firm.name} does not guarantee any particular result. Sending a demand letter does not stop or extend any statute of
    limitations or other legal deadline.
  </p>

  <h2>Jurisdiction</h2>
  <p>
    {firm.name} is a Florida law firm. This service is not available for every matter or in every jurisdiction. These
    terms are governed by the laws of the State of Florida.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${firm.email}`}>{firm.email}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
